{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler orchestrator \"stitch\" task (#5070) that requires implementing srd001-testutils R2.1-R2.4 in the go-unix-utils project. The specific goal is to replace the stub implementations of `RunDiffTests` and `BuildBinary` in `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` with functional code that executes Go and reference binaries with identical inputs, captures stdout/stderr/exit codes, compares outputs, and reports divergence. The task title is \"[stitch] srd001-testutils R2.1-R2.4 -- RunDiffTests binary execution and output comparison\". Only `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` should be modified. No git commands should be run. Code must compile and pass `go vet`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing: running a Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side with identical inputs\n   - `os/exec.Command` and `exec.CommandContext` for binary invocation with timeout\n   - `context.WithTimeout` for 10-second default timeout (R2.3)\n   - Environment variable merging with LC_ALL=C default (R2.6)\n   - `t.Run` subtests for individual DiffTest execution (R2.1)\n   - `*exec.ExitError` for extracting exit codes from process execution\n   - Normalization functions applied to output before comparison (R3.1)\n   - TimestampNormalizer using regexp for strftime patterns (R4.2)\n   - ExpectedFiles for file-output utilities like sponge (R5.1-R5.2)\n   - `t.Fatalf` on first divergence per SRD AC1\n   - Function size limit of 40 lines (E8), file size limit of 500 lines (E9)\n   - No imports of cmd/ or other pkg/ packages (D4)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD with all requirements R1-R5, acceptance criteria AC1-AC9\